{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01J7WWCbigV2yuXxiqnvC4gu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All tasks complete. Here's the acceptance criteria verification:\n\n**AC1** - `go build ./pkg/sys/...` compiles without errors on linux (verified above). Darwin compilation is ensured by separate `stat_darwin.go` with build constraint; all shared code uses cross-platform APIs.\n\n**AC2** - `FileInfo` struct in `stat.go:16-28` returns `ModTime` as `time.Time` and `Blocks` as `int64`. `Stat()` and `Lstat()` extract these from `os.FileInfo` + underlying `syscall.Stat_t` via platform-specific `fillFromStat`.\n\n**AC3** - `InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` in `signal.go:18-23` accepts SIGPIPE via `signal.Notify` and `OnTerminalResize()` in `signal.go:37-60` accepts SIGWINCH. Both use `os.Signal` values. `InstallSIGPIPEHandler` returns implicitly (goroutine runs in background); `OnTerminalResize` accepts a callback.\n\n**AC4** - `TerminalWidth()` in `terminal.go:16-21` returns `(int, error)` with rows=columns from `unix.IoctlGetWinsize(TIOCGWINSZ)`. `IsTerminal()` in `terminal.go:26-29` returns bool.\n\n**AC5** - Platform-specific code is in `stat_darwin.go` (with `//go:build darwin`) and `stat_linux.go` (with `//go:build linux`). These are the only files with platform-divergent syscall access (`Mtimespec` vs `Mtim`, type widths for `Dev`/`Rdev`/`Nlink`).\n\n**AC6** - All 6 `.go` files include the copyright header \"Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\" and \"SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\" on lines 1-2."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":405,"cache_read_input_tokens":63307,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":405},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5749d197-4955-4bd2-a1f1-74b483ba573f","uuid":"0